ari.djvu/page1-1920px-G%C3%B3d%C3%A1vari.djvu.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1920,"thumbheight":3243,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/G%C3%B3d%C3%A1vari.djvu/page1-1920px-G%C3%B3d%C3%A1vari.djvu.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1920,"height":3243},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/G%C3%B3d%C3%A1vari.djvu?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%B3d%C3%A1vari.djvu","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=64587667","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nMadras (India\u00a0: State)</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/vnd.djvu"}]},"57088265":{"pageid":57088265,"ns":6,"title":"File:Karoo Koppies Calvinia.jpg","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":1883344,"width":4000,"height":707,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg/1920px-Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1920,"thumbheight":339,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg/3840px-Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg/1920px-Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1920,"height":339,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg/3840px-Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karoo_Koppies_Calvinia.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=57088265","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Typical flat topped Karoo koppies (or hills/mountains) due to the erosion resistant horizontal layers of dolerite (subsurface lava) which were injected between the sedimentary strata of the Karoo Supergroup about 180 million years ago as an immediate prelude to the break-up of Gondwana. The soft sedimentary rocks have since then been eroded away to form a generally flat plain, interrupted by these koppies where the underlying shales were protected by a cap of dolerite. This range of mountains is known as the Keiskieberge, near Calvinia.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2017-02-28","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Oggmus\" title=\"User:Oggmus\">Oggmus</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},"30138932":{"pageid":30138932,"ns":6,"title":"File:Taylorglacier pho 2013 studinger.jpg","index":2,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":156393,"width":720,"height":480,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Taylorglacier_pho_2013_studinger.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":1920,"thumbheight":1280,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Taylorglacier_pho_2013_studinger.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1920,"height":1280},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Taylorglacier_pho_2013_studinger.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taylorglacier_pho_2013_studinger.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=30138932","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"While flying over Antarctica aboard a P-3 aircraft in November 2013, Operation IceBridge project scientist Michael Studinger took this photograph (top) of Taylor Valley, one of Antarctica\u2019s unique dry valleys. Home to Taylor Glacier, striking rock outcrops, and Blood Falls, the valley is one of the most remote and geologically exotic places in the world. \n<p>While ice and snow covers most of Antarctica, Taylor Valley and the other dry valleys are conspicuously bare. Inland mountains\u2014the Transantarctic Range\u2014force moisture out of the air as it passes over, leaving the valley in a precipitation shadow. The lack of precipitation leaves dramatic sequences of exposed rock. In both the satellite image and photograph, the tan bands are sandstone layers from the Beacon Supergroup, a series of sedimentary rock layers formed at the bottom of a shallow sea between 250 million and 400 million years ago. Throughout that period, Earth\u2019s southern continents were locked into the supercontinent Gondwana.\n</p><p>The dark band of rock that divides the sandstone is dolerite (sometimes called diabase), a volcanic rock that forms underground. The distinctive dolerite intrusion\u2014or sill\u2014is a remnant of a massive volcanic plumbing system that produced major eruptions about 180 million years ago. The eruptions likely helped tear Gondwana apart.\n</p>\nThe dominant feature in the photograph\u2014Taylor Glacier\u2014is notable as well. Like other glaciers in the Dry Valleys, it is \u201ccold-based,\u201d meaning its bottom is frozen to the ground below. The rest of the world\u2019s glaciers are \u201cwet-based,\u201d meaning they scrape over the bedrock, picking up and leaving obvious piles of debris (moraines) along their edges.\u20ac","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"acquired November 19, 2013","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Michael Studinger, NASA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},"50169866":{"pageid":50169866,"ns":6,"title":"File:The Imperial Gazetteer of India - Volume 6 (2nd edition).pdf","index":8,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":75084814,"width":556,"height":1160,"pagecount":792,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/The_Imperial_Gazetteer_of_India_-_Volume_6_%282nd_edition%29.pdf/page1-500px-The_Imperial_Gazetteer_of_India_-_Volume_6_%282nd_edition%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1920,"thumbheight":4006,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/The_Imperial_Gazetteer_of_India_-_Volume_6_%282nd_edition%29.pdf/page1-500px-The_Imperial_Gazetteer_of_India_-_Volume_6_%282nd_edition%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1920,"height":4006},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d4/The_Imperial_Gazetteer_of_India_-_Volume_6_%282nd_edition%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Imperial_Gazetteer_of_India_-_Volume_6_(2nd_edition).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=50169866","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:William_Wilson_Hunter\" class=\"extiw\" title=\